  "name": "Korean sinawi (shaman ensemble improvisation)",
  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Korean sinawi shamanic-ensemble improvisational tradition of southwestern Korea (Jeolla provinces and adjacent Chungcheong region), serving as the ritual-music accompaniment for the gut Korean shaman ceremony. Performance integrates a mudang shaman-priestess with an instrumental ensemble of daegeum bamboo flute, piri double-reed pipe, haegeum two-string fiddle, ajaeng bowed zither, and janggu hourglass-drum percussion in collective improvisational heterophony over the canonical sinawi modal-and-rhythmic framework. Distinguished from sanjo by sinawi's collective-ensemble (vs solo virtuoso) configuration; distinguished from pansori by sinawi's instrumental-ensemble (vs solo vocal narrative) framework. Direct historical ancestor of sanjo solo art-music.",
